      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Core Provider**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the file structure. I've decided to create `partial_results.py`. I have landed on Google Cloud Speech-to-Text as the concrete, external provider to use for this project. The goal is to define its usage and make it clearly identifiable in the codebase.\n\n\n**Implementing Partial Results**\n\nI'm focusing now on implementing the `partial_results.py` file. I'll use the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text streaming API with the `google.cloud.speech` library. I'm building a function in that file to process `StreamingRecognizeResponse` objects and extract both partial and final recognition results, clearly differentiating between them in the output. This is a critical step.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864345152,
          "start": 1789864343860
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc3a7934001t4yy6gYm6lX71R",
