      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Streaming Source**\n\nI'm solidifying the foundation of `stream_chunks.py`. My focus is zeroing in on an external provider for audio chunk streaming; Google Cloud Speech-to-Text feels like a strong choice for the speech-to-text aspect. It's key to make this selection explicit in the code for clarity.\n\n\n**Refining the Streaming Implementation**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the client-side logic within `stream_chunks.py`. My primary objective is creating an async generator for audio chunks, which the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API will receive as `StreamingRecognizeRequest` objects. I'm prioritizing the chunk sending mechanism, making the API integration explicit. I'll defer the actual audio chunk generation. I'm focusing on defining the `stream_chunks.py` file with necessary imports.\n\n\n**Structuring the Chunk Stream**\n\nI'm now concretizing the implementation steps for `stream_chunks.py`. I'm starting by importing the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text SDK and establishing a basic async function. I'm focusing on the provider's integration to send audio chunks. I'll define an async generator to yield `StreamingRecognizeRequest` objects and handle the `client.streaming_recognize` call with the config and generator. The actual audio capture is deferred; I'm simulating chunk provision. I'm making sure to define and create the necessary `SpeechClient`, `RecognitionConfig`, and `StreamingRecognitionConfig`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864341777,
          "start": 1789864337180
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc3a5f1c001pbaZFxBDlts2x8",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc3a5a41001hBLLMlz1cF0k5k",
      "session_id": "ses_f43c5a5cfffez6fM4tw43fgrtB",
      "time_created": 1789864337180,
      "time_updated": 1789864341778
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "o929X7NO10hCtht7",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import asyncio\nfrom google.cloud import speech_v1p1beta1 as speech\n\nasync def stream_audio_chunks(audio_source):\n    \"\"\"\n    Streams audio chunks from an asynchronous source to Google Cloud Speech-to-Text.\n\n    Args:\n        audio_source: An asynchronous generator or iterable that yields raw audio bytes.\n                      For example, an async function reading from a microphone or a file.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = speech.SpeechClient()\n\n    config = speech.RecognitionConfig(\n        encoding=speech.RecognitionConfig.AudioEncoding.LINEAR16,\n        sample_rate_hertz=16000,\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n    )\n\n    streaming_config = speech.StreamingRecognitionConfig(\n        config=config,\n        interim_results=True,\n    )\n\n    # An async generator that yields StreamingRecognizeRequest objects\n    async def request_generator():\n        # The first request must contain the streaming configuration\n        yield speech.StreamingRecognizeRequest(streaming_config=streaming_config)\n\n        async for chunk in audio_source:\n            yield speech.StreamingRecognizeRequest(audio_content=chunk)\n\n    responses = client.streaming_recognize(config=streaming_config, requests=request_generator())\n\n    async for response in responses:\n        # Process the streaming recognition response\n        # For example, print interim and final transcripts\n        for result in response.results:\n            if result.is_final:\n                print(f\"Final transcript: {result.alternatives[0].transcript}\")\n            else:\n                print(f\"Interim transcript: {result.alternatives[0].transcript}\")\n\n",
            "filePath": "stream_chunks.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
